 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "sukkah.29a.7",
   "daf": "29a",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "מָשָׁל לְמָה הַדָּבָר דּוֹמֶה. אִיבַּעְיָא לְהוּ: מִי שָׁפַךְ לְמִי? תָּא שְׁמַע דְּתַנְיָא: שָׁפַךְ לוֹ רַבּוֹ קִיתוֹן עַל פָּנָיו, וְאָמַר לוֹ: אִי אֶפְשִׁי בְּשִׁמּוּשֶׁךָ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna continues: The Sages «told a parable: To what is this matter comparable?» It is comparable to a servant who comes to pour wine for his master, and he pours a jug of water in his face. «A dilemma was raised before» the Sages: «Who poured» the water «in whose» face? «Come» and «hear» a proof, «as it is taught» explicitly in a baraita: «His master poured a jug» of water «on his face and said to him: I do not want your service.»"
  }
 ],
